WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.309
So why not borrow Euclidean convolution for graphs?

00:00:03.389 --> 00:00:06.101
Convolution is sensitive to spatial order,

00:00:06.181 --> 00:00:09.357
but graph networks must be permutation invariant.

00:00:09.437 --> 00:00:14.143
Earlier methods picked a node ordering
independently of the convolution,

00:00:14.223 --> 00:00:18.463
so it could not be tuned for the task and often
lost information.

00:00:18.543 --> 00:00:23.580
What is missing is an ordering that is
differentiable and learned end to end.
